# Terraform Workflow Gates

## Plan before apply
Always run `terraform plan -out terraform_plans/{datetime}.tfplan` before any apply. Never run `terraform apply` without a saved plan file. The plan file is evidence of intent and enables safe, reviewable applies.

## PR gate
Attach plan output to every pull request. Apply only after the PR has been merged. Never run `terraform apply` on feature branches — branches are for review, not for applying infrastructure changes.

## Destroy protection
Never run `terraform destroy` yourself. Flag any resource that needs to be removed and document the reason. Let the human operator review and apply the destroy. If a resource block must be removed from code, use `removed {}` blocks or coordinate with the team.

## Drift detection
Schedule weekly `terraform plan` runs against production without applying. Treat any drift (unexpected differences between state and actual infrastructure) as a bug to be investigated and resolved before it compounds.

## Init every time
Run `terraform init` for new modules and after any changes to `versions.tf` or `required_providers` blocks. Never assume a previous init is still valid after provider or module version changes.
